174
00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:45.440
joan velja: One,

175
00:29:45.590 --> 00:29:53.749
joan velja: We probably want to red team as much as possible and audit channels of communication, namely listing every path that one agent can write.

176
00:29:53.910 --> 00:30:11.169
joan velja: and another one can read. Repos, caches, wikis, DNSs, CIs. OpenAI is now actively, for example, red-teaming all these routes to enforce stricter oversight in their internal mechanisms.

177
00:30:11.360 --> 00:30:18.670
joan velja: Intent monitoring, namely, sort of, full chain of thought monitoring, as opposed to, sort of, only action… only action monitoring.

178
00:30:19.300 --> 00:30:36.740
joan velja: as an example for this, the OpenAI sort of DNS monitor read the failed attempts, that one of the incidents was, trying to do as evidence that nothing really happened, just the agent, sort of, screwing up the DNS,

