322
00:48:34.070 --> 00:48:42.160
Kamil - Team Apart: If the mains channel's clean, but the receiver acts on info it shouldn't have. Can you detect side channel use from that mismatch?

323
00:48:42.530 --> 00:48:45.379
Kamil - Team Apart: Like, as opposed from the main channel itself?

324
00:48:46.100 --> 00:48:53.469
joan velja: Yeah, so the thing is, the channel is the same. The channel is unique, in the sense that there's only a main channel.

325
00:48:54.080 --> 00:48:59.810
joan velja: But the sender learns to use that main channel to embed.

326
00:48:59.960 --> 00:49:04.399
joan velja: quote-unquote, side-channel information. And so that's the…

327
00:49:04.640 --> 00:49:12.039
joan velja: That's the essence of, like, Stegonography itself, in the sense that there's no decoupling of the two informations, they're coupled into the same channel, and…

328
00:49:12.210 --> 00:49:17.070
joan velja: Only, sort of, decoded once they're past the monitor.

329
00:49:17.410 --> 00:49:27.099
